  "description": "issue #792: `tell [ :a :b ]` then a single `left 90` applies once per addressed turtle, emitting one `turn` per turtle carrying its own `turtle_id` (1 then 2) — `left` turns counter-clockwise from the default heading `0`, wrapping to `270` (spec/execution-model.md's counter-clockwise convention and `[0,360)` normalization). No `move`/`draw-segment` fires: turning does not change position. The events are stamped because the addressed set is now explicit (a `tell` has run). Every change of the addressed set — here from `tell` — also emits the addressing `primitive` event carrying `addressing: { addressed_turtle_ids, current_turtle_id }` (issue #766, spec/rendering.md:193). Closes the `left` execution-coverage gap the Sprites Epic Gate recorded (issue #792): `left` shares the `runPerTurtleCommand` loop and its turn-command dispatch predicate with `right`, but had no Sprites-addressed execution fixture of its own.",
